4. Notice by finder of treasure. Whenever any treasure exceeding in amount or value ten rupees is found, the finder shall, as soon as practicable, give to the Collector notice in writing___
(a) of the nature and amount or approximate value of such treasure;
(b) of the place in which it was found;

